quran[8]{c,v,t}:
  30,25,"And among His signs is that the heavens and the earth persist by His command. Then, when He calls you out of the earth with a single call, behold, you will come forth."
  30,26,And to Him belongs whoever is in the heavens and the earth. All are submissive to Him.
  30,27,"It is He Who originates the creation and then returns it—which is even easier for Him. To Him belongs the most exalted description in the heavens and the earth. And He is the All-Mighty, the All-Wise."
  30,28,He sets forth for you an example relating to yourselves. Do you have among your slaves any partners (whom you may allow to share) in whatever We have provided you so that you may become equal in its respect and that you may fear them as you fear each other? That is how We make the signs clear for people who understand.
  30,29,"Rather, the wrongdoers merely follow their desires without any knowledge. Who then can guide those whom Allah led astray? And they shall have no helpers."
  30,30,"So, set your face (and heart) steadfastly to the faith in an upright and pure state—the natural way made by Allah upon which He has originated humankind. Let there be no change in the creation of Allah; that is the upright religion. But most people do not know."
  30,31,"(Always) keep turning to Him in repentance. Be conscious of Him, establish the prayer, and be not among the polytheists."
  30,32,(And do not be like) those who divided their religion and split into sects—each faction rejoicing in what they have.
